title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf log revert
catalog: CLI command
target: mf log revert
summary: Undo a revision (or an operation) by writing its inverse at HEAD

!! Reference

```
Undo a revision (or an operation) by writing its inverse at HEAD

Usage: mf log revert [OPTIONS] [ARGS]...

Arguments:
  [ARGS]...
          "plan" to preview, optionally a revision id; or a revision id

Options:
      --op <OP>
          Revert this operation only (repeatable)

      --with-dependents
          Also revert whatever blocks the target (its dependency closure)

      --metadata-only
          Leave out the operations needing a filesystem action

      --label <LABEL>
          Label the revision the revert creates

      --on-move-available <ON_MOVE_AVAILABLE>
          Policy when the file is present: apply|skip|abort|ask (default apply)

      --on-move-unavailable <ON_MOVE_UNAVAILABLE>
          Policy when the file is missing: apply|skip|abort|ask (default ask)

      --force
          Skip the confirmation prompt

      --silent
          Suppress informational output

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
